  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Mitigating vulnerabilities and addressing humanitarian needs of refugees and migrants from Myanmar, in particular Rohingya undertaking maritime andland movements in Indonesia, Thailand and Malaysia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Complex mobility flows remain a dominant feature in the region, stemming from the ongoing multi-dimensional crisis in Myanmar. The systematic human rights violations against the Rohingya people and the February 2021 military takeover in Myanmar have forced people to flee the country, and seek refuge in neighbouring countries including Malaysia, Indonesia and Thailand. This, combined with both the increasing risk of famine as well as the forced conscription of Rohingya in Myanmar has led to an increase in maritime and land movements to neighbouring countries. Through this action, IOM provides multi-sectoral assistance for the benefit of Rohingya refugees. Sectoral assistance includes Health, Non-Food Items, Water, Sanitation and Hygiene, Shelter, Protection and multi-purpose cash grants to new arrivals and residual caseloads. IOM continues to gather, analyze and share data on complex mobility in the region with a particular focus on land and maritime movements of Rohingya refugees and cross-border mobility between Myanmar and Thailand, building on the robust methodology developed previously. This information will be used to guide the delivery of assistance and serve as the evidence base to develop advocacy to inform decision making of humanitarian agencies and policy at regional and national levels.</narrative>
  </description>
